# Review and delegation tooling for this repo

<!-- boardkit-contract: v2 -->

This file is a per-project fill-in, not a generic doc. It pins the actual
tools and harness bindings this repo uses for review and delegation, so a
board owner does not have to rediscover tool mechanics every session. Cards
cite this file instead of repeating it.

A repo's `REVIEW-TOOLING.md` overrides any generic delegation-skill guidance
a harness might load by default. If a skill's default instructions conflict
with what is pinned here, this file wins.

## The standing rule

Code changes retain the independent Gate A review defined in `PROCESS.md`
and `MODEL-CLASSES.md`, using a capable programming-language-specific
code-review agent. Run it in the board owner's harness when an eligible
reviewer is available; otherwise use an approved independent model or defer.
Offer optional Frontier plan review: the user may accept, decline or name
a substitute before dispatch. Other non-code artifacts follow their agreed
task gates. Prose format alone creates no review gate and does not select
`general` as a technical reviewer.

An adversarial review of a standalone prose artifact that is not a card (a
plan, an ADR, a design doc) appends a numbered findings ledger to the
artifact itself, so the record travels with it. The ledger carries an
explicit verdict and names both the author model and the reviewer model.
Each finding records its disposition: the fix applied, or the reason the
finding was rejected. An empty or verdict-less return is a failed review,
never a clean pass. Zero findings is recorded as an explicit PASS,
distinguishable from a tool that silently returned nothing.

## Fix-round packets

The review-slot policy in PROCESS.md determines whether a repair needs a
reviewer or owner verification. A new commit alone does not require another
dispatch. Extend the card's range and preserve exact candidate evidence
either way; a substantive re-review gets the full-range packet plus the
prior findings and dispositions.

Stage role-specific review material at `.review/<card>/<role>/` in the
base repo, not an execution worktree. Use the existing `boardkit review-packet`
command for scripted diff capture, then assemble the role packet without
destroying prior receipts. Its configured output directory remains the
legacy generator output; this convention does not add a role flag or
change receipt lookup. Keep the source worktree and SHA/range explicit.
The `--repo` override selects the worktree to inspect; `--suffix` remains
the discriminator for a supplementary or second-repo packet.

